+# swarmagents-vm-desktop
+
+The SwarmAgents VM image: a Debian bookworm (node 22) container with a
+headless desktop, VNC access, a persistent Chromium with remote debugging,
+and the Claude Code CLI — the baseline for a real agent to watch and drive
+a computer.
+
+## What's inside
+
+| Component | Detail |
+| --- | --- |
+| Base | `node:22-bookworm-slim` (Debian bookworm + Node 22) |
+| Display server | Xvfb on `:1` at 1280x800x24 |
+| Window manager / taskbar | openbox + tint2 (bottom taskbar) |
+| Wallpaper | gradient PNG set with feh on startup |
+| VNC | x11vnc on `127.0.0.1:5900`, no password (only proxyable via websockify) |
+| Web VNC | websockify + noVNC (Debian `novnc` package) serving on `0.0.0.0:6080`, page at `/vnc.html` |
+| Browser | Chromium, persistent, running as `agent` on `:1`, remote debugging on `127.0.0.1:9222`, profile at `/home/agent/.chromium` |
+| Tooling | git, curl, python3, build-essential, tmux |
+| Agent CLI | Claude Code (`@anthropic-ai/claude-code` → `/usr/local/bin/claude`) |
+| User | non-root `agent` (uid 1000), `HOME=/home/agent`, `/workspace` owned by agent |
+| Entrypoint | tiny supervisor: restarts any of Xvfb / openbox / tint2 / x11vnc / websockify / Chromium that dies; sleeps forever; TERM/INT-clean |
+
+## Build
+
+```bash
+scripts/build-vm-image.sh
+```
+
+Produces `swarmagents-vm-desktop:latest`. There is also a `--smoke-test`
+flag that builds, boots a throwaway container, and runs the acceptance
+checks automatically.
+
+## Run
+
+```bash
+docker run -d -p 6080:6080 swarmagents-vm-desktop
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:6080/vnc.html — you should see the desktop with
+Chromium. (The VNC handshake is password-less; the x11vnc listener binds to
+loopback inside the container, so it is only reachable through the
+websockify proxy on 6080.)
+
+Checks inside the container:
+
+```bash
+docker exec -u agent <c> claude --version   # Claude Code CLI
+docker exec <c> xdpyinfo -display :1        # X server up
+curl http://127.0.0.1:9222/json/version      # Chromium DevTools endpoint
+```
+
+## Ports
+
+| Port | Binding | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 6080 | `0.0.0.0` | noVNC web client + websockify proxy (publish this one) |
+| 5900 | `127.0.0.1` | x11vnc (loopback only) |
+| 9222 | `127.0.0.1` | Chromium remote debugging (loopback only) |
+
+## Image size
+
+~2.07 GB (2,068,705,914 bytes) on disk as reported by `docker images`
+/ `docker image inspect`. The bulk is Chromium, the X/VNC stack, build
+tooling and Claude Code. If size matters, the smallest high-impact cuts:
+drop `build-essential` (only needed for agents that compile) and
+`imagemagick` (only used at build time to generate the wallpaper — the
+PNG could be committed instead).
+
+## Notes
+
+- The entrypoint runs as `agent` (`USER agent` in the Dockerfile); the
+  supervisor restarts services with its PID-tracking loop. Xvfb uses
+  `-ac` (no access control) because every client is either loopback or in
+  the container — the published surface is only the noVNC page on 6080.
+- Chromium runs with `--no-sandbox` (container-friendly) and
+  `--disable-dev-shm-usage` (small `/dev/shm` in docker).
+- The `agent` user is uid 1000, matching the host volume mounted at
+  `/workspace` by the swarm VM driver.
diff --git a/apps/swarmagents/vm-image/entrypoint.sh b/apps/swarmagents/vm-image/entrypoint.sh
new file mode 100755
index 000000000..c017910e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/swarmagents/vm-image/entrypoint.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,197 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+#
+# entrypoint.sh — swarmagents-vm-desktop supervisor.
+#
+# Starts and then keeps running (restarting anything that dies):
+#   Xvfb :1 (1280x800x24) → openbox (WM) + tint2 (taskbar) + wallpaper
+#   x11vnc on 127.0.0.1:5900 (no password; only reachable via websockify)
+#   websockify + noVNC on 0.0.0.0:6080
+#   Chromium (as the agent user) with remote debugging on 127.0.0.1:9222
+#
+# Runs forever. Signal-friendly: TERM/INT stop it cleanly, so `docker stop`
+# works with or without --init/tini.
+set -euo pipefail
+
+export HOME=/home/agent
+export DISPLAY=:1
+X_SCREEN="1280x800x24"
+WALLPAPER="$HOME/wallpaper.png"
+
+log() { echo "$(date -Is) [vm-desktop] $*"; }
+
+# ── X server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+start_xvfb() {
+  log "starting Xvfb on ${DISPLAY} (${X_SCREEN})"
+  Xvfb "${DISPLAY}" -screen 0 "${X_SCREEN}" -ac -noreset \
+    >/tmp/xvfb.log 2>&1 &
+  XVFB_PID=$!
+}
+
+wait_for_x() {
+  for _ in $(seq 1 100); do
+    if xdpyinfo -display "${DISPLAY}" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+      return 0
+    fi
+    sleep 0.2
+  done
+  log "X server did not come up; exiting" >&2
+  exit 1
+}
+
+# ── desktop (WM + taskbar + wallpaper) ──────────────────────────────────────
+setup_openbox() {
+  local cfg="$HOME/.config/openbox/rc.xml"
+  mkdir -p "$(dirname "$cfg")"
+  if [ ! -f "$cfg" ]; then
+    cat > "$cfg" <<'XML'
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<openbox_config xmlns="http://openbox.org/3.4/rc">
+  <theme><name>Clearlooks</name></theme>
+  <desktops>
+    <number>1</number>
+    <names><name>Desktop</name></names>
+  </desktops>
+  <resistance><slop>0</slop><edge>0</edge></resistance>
+</openbox_config>
+XML
+  fi
+}
+
+setup_tint2() {
+  local cfg="$HOME/.config/tint2/tint2rc"
+  mkdir -p "$(dirname "$cfg")"
+  if [ ! -f "$cfg" ]; then
+    cat > "$cfg" <<'RC'
+# Tint2 taskbar (default generated by the VM entrypoint)
+rounded = 0
+border_width = 0
+border_sides = L R T B
+border_content_bg = false
+background_color = #1b1f27 95
+border_color = #3a3f4b 100
+
+rounded = 2
+border_width = 0
+border_sides = L R T B
+border_content_bg = false
+background_color = #2f3542 100
+border_color = #5c6474 100
+
+rounded = 2
+border_width = 0
+border_sides = L R T B
+border_content_bg = false
+background_color = #262b36 80
+border_color = #454b59 100
+
+panel_items = LTSC
+panel_size = 100% 32
+panel_margin = 0 0
+panel_padding = 2 2
+panel_background_id = 1
+panel_layer = top
+panel_position = bottom center
+panel_monitor = all
+panel_shrink = 0
+autohide = 0
+
+taskbar_mode = single_desktop
+taskbar_hide_if_empty = 0
+taskbar_always_show_all_desktops = 1
+
+task_icon = 1
+task_text = 1
+task_centered = 0
+task_maximum_size = 200 28
+task_padding = 4 2
+task_background_id = 3
+task_active_background_id = 2
+task_font_color = #c9cdd6 100
+task_active_font_color = #ffffff 100
+task_icon_size = 20
+
+time1_format = %H:%M
+time1_font = sans 10
+clock_font_color = #c9cdd6 100
+clock_padding = 6 0
+clock_background_id = 0
+RC
+  fi
+}
+
+start_wm() {
+  setup_openbox
+  setup_tint2
+  log "setting wallpaper (feh)"
+  feh --bg-fill "$WALLPAPER" || true
+  log "starting openbox"
+  openbox >/tmp/openbox.log 2>&1 &
+  WM_PID=$!
+}
+
+start_tint2() {
+  log "starting tint2 taskbar"
+  tint2 >/tmp/tint2.log 2>&1 &
+  TINT2_PID=$!
+}
+
+# ── VNC + noVNC ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+start_vnc() {
+  log "starting x11vnc on 127.0.0.1:5900 (no password)"
+  x11vnc -display "${DISPLAY}" -forever -shared -nopw -listen 127.0.0.1 \
+    -rfbport 5900 >/tmp/x11vnc.log 2>&1 &
+  VNC_PID=$!
+}
+
+start_websockify() {
+  log "starting websockify/noVNC on 0.0.0.0:6080"
+  websockify --web /usr/share/novnc 0.0.0.0:6080 localhost:5900 \
+    >/tmp/websockify.log 2>&1 &
+  WEBSOCKIFY_PID=$!
+}
+
+# ── browser (persistent Chromium with remote debugging) ─────────────────────
+start_chromium() {
+  log "starting chromium with remote debugging on 127.0.0.1:9222"
+  chromium --no-sandbox --disable-gpu --disable-dev-shm-usage \
+    --window-size=1280,800 \
+    --remote-debugging-address=127.0.0.1 \
+    --remote-debugging-port=9222 \
+    --user-data-dir="$HOME/.chromium" \
+    about:blank >/tmp/chromium.log 2>&1 &
+  CHROMIUM_PID=$!
+}
+
+# ── supervisor loop ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# Check liveness via /proc: bash keeps exited background children around as
+# zombies until waited on, so `kill -0` would count a dead service as alive.
+alive() {
+  local pid="$1" state
+  [ -d "/proc/$pid" ] || return 1
+  state="$(awk '{print $3}' "/proc/$pid/stat" 2>/dev/null)" || return 1
+  [ "$state" != "Z" ]
+}
+
+# Stop cleanly on `docker stop` (with or without tini/--init).
+trap 'log "shutting down"; exit 0' TERM INT
+
+start_xvfb
+wait_for_x
+start_wm
+start_tint2
+start_vnc
+start_websockify
+start_chromium
+
+while true; do
+  if ! alive "$XVFB_PID"; then
+    start_xvfb
+    wait_for_x
+  fi
+  alive "$WM_PID" || start_wm
+  alive "$TINT2_PID" || start_tint2
+  alive "$VNC_PID" || start_vnc
+  alive "$WEBSOCKIFY_PID" || start_websockify
+  alive "$CHROMIUM_PID" || start_chromium
+  sleep 2
+done
